/*
 * Hashtag Scoring System:
 * Each hashtag is scored out of 30 based on three criteria (0-10 each):
 * - Popularity (P): X usage/trending potential, based on 2023-2024 data from Statista (Congress hashtags), Hootsuite (social media trends), and Brand24 (X insights).
 *   - 8-10: Millions of uses or top trends (e.g., #News, #Crypto)
 *   - 5-7: Thousands of uses, niche but active (e.g., #Veterans, #RenewableEnergy)
 *   - 1-4: Low traction, highly specific (e.g., #FAA)
 * - Relevance (R): Tie to U.S. legislation/bills, based on congressional topics.
 *   - 8-10: Core bill topics (e.g., #Healthcare, #Taxes)
 *   - 5-7: Related but narrower (e.g., #Drought, #ChildCare)
 *   - 1-4: Tangential (e.g., #Heritage)
 * - Broad Appeal (B): General X audience draw, beyond niche groups.
 *   - 8-10: Universal interest (e.g., #USA, #Jobs)
 *   - 5-7: Moderate appeal (e.g., #PublicSafety, #Innovation)
 *   - 1-4: Hyper-specific (e.g., #FAA)
 * Total Score = P + R + B, minimum 18/30 for inclusion.
 * Sources: Statista (2023), Hootsuite (2024), Brand24 (2024), projected to March 2025 for evergreen/trending relevance.
 */
